cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "walkforward-engine"
abstract: >-
  A bot-agnostic walk-forward analysis engine for trading strategies. Provides rolling
  walk-forward optimization with blind out-of-sample scoring, an absolute survival gate built on
  scale-free statistics (Probabilistic Sharpe Ratio), Monte Carlo path risk including probability
  of ruin, and selection-overfit backstops (PBO via CSCV, and trial-deflated Sharpe).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Levy"
    given-names: "Yaniv"
repository-code: "https://github.com/oager/walkforward-engine"
url: "https://github.com/oager/walkforward-engine"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
keywords:
  - walk-forward analysis
  - backtesting
  - overfitting
  - probabilistic sharpe ratio
  - deflated sharpe ratio
  - monte carlo
  - quantitative finance
  - out-of-sample validation
